# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — COMPLETE PRODUCTION-READY MULTILINGUAL APPLICATION

## 1. YOUR ROLE AND PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, software architect, UI/UX designer, database engineer, AI integration specialist, localization engineer, and QA tester.

Build a **complete, functional, production-oriented application in one implementation**, following every requirement below.

Do not merely generate a landing page, static dashboard, UI mockup, or collection of disconnected screens. Implement the application end to end, including navigation, business logic, data persistence, form validation, API integration where required, error handling, loading states, empty states, authentication if specified, and complete multilingual support.

The finished result must be a usable application in which every visible button, form, menu, navigation item, selector, filter, and action performs its intended function.

### Core rules

1. Build the actual application, not a visual demonstration.
2. Implement the complete user journey, from the first screen to the final result.
3. Connect every screen to real application state and working logic.
4. Persist important data using an appropriate database or local storage mechanism.
5. Do not use fake success messages, hardcoded dynamic results, or simulated backend responses as substitutes for required functionality.
6. Where a third-party service requires API credentials, implement the actual integration interface, secure configuration, validation, and useful setup instructions. Never fabricate API keys.
7. If an external service is unavailable, display an honest, understandable error and provide a suitable fallback where possible.
8. Preserve existing project functionality when working inside an existing codebase. Do not rewrite unrelated features unnecessarily.
9. Avoid unnecessary complexity, redundant dependencies, and placeholder features.
10. Prioritize a stable, usable, responsive, and maintainable final application over decorative effects.

