## 9. ACCESSIBILITY AND USABILITY

Make the application usable by people with different accessibility needs.

- Use readable text and sufficient contrast.
- Provide accessible labels for interactive controls.
- Support keyboard navigation where relevant.
- Use semantic headings and controls.
- Provide meaningful error messages.
- Do not rely on color alone to communicate status.
- Ensure dialogs and menus can be operated accessibly.
- Support screen readers using the appropriate platform conventions.
- Ensure localized text remains accessible.
- Respect system font scaling where possible.

Accessibility must work across all six supported languages.

